From fb7e8f8e4d85805325251120f41afb345ecd7613 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Struan Bartlett <struan.bartlett@NewsNow.co.uk>
Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 02:02:49 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 07/10] passthrough: Keep a cache policy per inode

Add InodeData::cache_policy, the cache policy of the mount the inode is
on, with None standing for the file system's default policy, and take
the FOPEN_* flags and the entry/attribute timeouts of every reply from
it.  Nothing sets it yet, so there is no change in behaviour.

do_open() now resolves the inode once, before opening it, and uses the
same InodeData for the open flags.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 .../device_state/deserialization.rs           |  3 ++
 .../preserialization/find_paths.rs            |  1 +
 src/passthrough/inode_store.rs                |  4 ++
 src/passthrough/mod.rs                        | 39 ++++++++++++++-----
 4 files changed, 38 insertions(+), 9 deletions(-)

